  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "On turn 1 with a land drop remaining and two Forests in hand, the player passed priority in the postcombat main phase without playing a land. This wastes the entire turn's land drop, putting them a full turn behind on mana development. With a hand full of 2-3 mana creatures (Ironshell Beetle, Duskshell Crawler, Lightning Visionary), missing this land drop delays everything by a turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in postcombat main phase without playing a Forest.",
      "better_line": "Play a Forest to have 1 mana available next turn, enabling a turn 2 two-drop like Ironshell Beetle or Duskshell Crawler.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 6,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 16,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Player timed out and failed to play a land or cast any spell during their precombat main phase on turn 6. They had Evolving Wilds and two Forests available to play as their land drop, and with Thriving Grove (which can produce white) plus any land played, they could have cast Kami of Ancient Law (1W). Playing Evolving Wilds would also trigger Turntimber Basilisk's landfall when eventually cast, and help fix mana. Missing an entire turn's land drop and spell cast is a significant tempo loss.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out (no response), passing priority without playing a land or casting anything.",
      "better_line": "Play Evolving Wilds (or Forest), then potentially cast Kami of Ancient Law using Thriving Grove for W and a Forest for the generic cost, developing the board against the opponent's growing threats.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 49,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 39,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Attempted to cast Kami of Ancient Law for {1}{W} but couldn't complete the mana payment, likely because Thriving Grove was not set to white. With Divine Verdict, Kami of Ancient Law, and Midnight Guard all requiring white mana in hand, the Thriving Grove should have been set to white when it entered. The failed cast attempt also delays playing a land (Evolving Wilds to search for a Plains) which would help fix their mana.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Kami of Ancient Law, which was rolled back due to inability to pay white mana.",
      "better_line": "Play Evolving Wilds first, sacrifice it to search for a Plains (fixing white mana for future turns), then pass. The Thriving Grove should have been set to white when it entered earlier, given the heavy white requirements in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 49,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 39,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Attacking with Oashra Cultivator, a 0/3 creature, deals 0 damage to the opponent. This accomplishes nothing offensively while tapping the Cultivator, removing it as a potential blocker. The opponent has a 1/4 Duskshell Crawler with trample that will be able to attack next turn, and the 0/3 Cultivator could serve as a useful blocker.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with Oashra Cultivator (0/3), dealing 0 damage and tapping it unnecessarily.",
      "better_line": "Don't attack with the 0/3 Oashra Cultivator. Keep it untapped as a potential blocker against the opponent's Duskshell Crawler (1/4 with trample) or to use its sacrifice ability in future turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 55,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 43,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Timed out on Thriving Grove color choice, likely defaulting to White instead of Red. QwCdr Proud has Borderland Minotaur and Lightning Visionary in hand requiring red mana, with no red sources on board. Choosing the wrong color wastes the primary mana-fixing purpose of Thriving Grove.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out, defaulting to White (or whatever the default is) instead of actively choosing Red.",
      "better_line": "Choose Red for Thriving Grove to enable casting Borderland Minotaur and Lightning Visionary.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 83,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 55,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Lightning Visionary is a 2/1 with prowess but the hand is almost entirely creatures (only Crawling Sensation as a noncreature spell), making prowess nearly irrelevant. Giant Ladybug would be a 4/1 with reach that also tutors a basic land to the top of the library, which is very relevant given the expensive hand (Borderland Minotaur at {2}{R}{R}, Moldgraf Millipede at {4}{G}, Nantuko Cultivator at {3}{G}) and no land in hand.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Lightning Visionary (2/1 prowess with few triggers)",
      "better_line": "Cast Giant Ladybug to get a 4/1 reach body and tutor a land to the top of library, ensuring the next land drop and enabling the expensive spells in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 119,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 77,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Blocked the 1/1 Ironshell Beetle with the valuable Turntimber Basilisk (2/1 deathtouch), trading it for a much less valuable creature. The Basilisk dies to the 1/1's combat damage (1 toughness) while only killing a 1/1. Taking 1 damage would have been far preferable to losing the deathtouch creature.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked Duskshell Crawler with Midnight Guard and Ironshell Beetle with Turntimber Basilisk, losing both blockers.",
      "better_line": "Block only Duskshell Crawler with Midnight Guard (still the best trampler block), and let the 1/1 Ironshell Beetle through for 1 damage. Preserving Turntimber Basilisk's deathtouch for future combat is worth far more than preventing 1 damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 133,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 84,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to activate Evolving Wilds when it was the only available action and would have provided free value: fetching a basic land (likely Plains for future white spells like Divine Verdict, Kami of Ancient Law, Valorous Stance in hand), deck thinning, and an additional Landfall trigger on Turntimber Basilisk.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and passed without activating Evolving Wilds",
      "better_line": "Activate Evolving Wilds to fetch a Plains, enabling future white spell casting and getting an extra Landfall trigger",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 148,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 90,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Missed activating Evolving Wilds during combat to trigger Turntimber Basilisk's Landfall ability, which would force Lightning Visionary (2/1) to block the deathtouch Basilisk, trading it off. This wastes a significant synergy between Evolving Wilds and the Basilisk's Landfall + deathtouch.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Evolving Wilds during combat.",
      "better_line": "Activate Evolving Wilds to fetch a basic land, triggering Turntimber Basilisk's Landfall to force Lightning Visionary to block it. The deathtouch Basilisk would kill the Visionary, removing a threat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 160,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 95,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Turntimber Basilisk's landfall ability forces a creature to block the deathtouch Basilisk. While the Basilisk is tapped and unlikely to attack this turn (making the choice largely moot), targeting Ironshell Beetle (a 1/1 that already used its ETB) is the worst option. Giant Ladybug (4/1) is the highest-value target to force into a deathtouch block.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Ironshell Beetle (1/1) with Turntimber Basilisk's landfall forced-block ability",
      "better_line": "Target Giant Ladybug (4/1) - the most threatening creature on the opponent's board - to force it into a lethal block against the deathtouch Basilisk if it attacks",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 177,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 110,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Llama4 Rules declined to block when Midnight Guard (2/3) could have blocked and killed Lightning Visionary (2/1) for free (Midnight Guard survives). This lets a prowess creature live and deals 2 unnecessary damage. Oashra Cultivator could also have chump-blocked the Ironshell Beetle to prevent 1 more damage.",
      "action_taken": "No blocks declared, taking 3 damage from Ironshell Beetle and Lightning Visionary.",
      "better_line": "Block Lightning Visionary with Midnight Guard to kill the Visionary for free (Midnight Guard survives at 2/3 vs 2/1). This removes a threat and saves 2 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 191,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 117,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Kami of Ancient Law (2/2 with no enchantment targets) instead of Canopy Baloth (4/3 with landfall). The opponent's board is mostly tapped, making this an ideal window to deploy the larger threat. Playing a land after Baloth would make it a 6/5 attacker. Kami's enchantment-destruction ability has no current target.",
