      "decision_index": 121,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Opponent has no available blockers (Giant Ladybug is summoning sick, Ironshell Beetle and Lightning Visionary are tapped), so attacking with both Midnight Guard and Turntimber Basilisk would deal 4 damage instead of 2 with zero risk.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only Turntimber Basilisk (2/1) for 2 damage.",
      "better_line": "Attack with both Midnight Guard (2/3) and Turntimber Basilisk (2/1) for 4 total unblockable damage, since the opponent has no available blockers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 210,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 127,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Declined to block Turntimber Basilisk (2/1 deathtouch with landfall forced-block ability) with Giant Ladybug (4/1). The Basilisk's deathtouch means it trades with anything that blocks it, and Giant Ladybug's 1 toughness means it will die to almost any interaction anyway. Trading a fragile 4/1 for a persistent deathtouch threat with a dangerous landfall ability is generally favorable, especially since the Basilisk can force future blocks and kill better creatures.",
      "action_taken": "Did not block, taking 2 damage (14→12 life) and leaving Turntimber Basilisk alive.",
      "better_line": "Block Turntimber Basilisk with Giant Ladybug to trade the fragile 4/1 for the deathtouch creature, preventing future landfall-forced blocks that could kill more valuable creatures like Sethron or Moldgraf Millipede.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 213,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 128,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Blocked Lightning Visionary (3/2) with Midnight Guard (2/3) instead of Giant Ladybug (4/1). Giant Ladybug has only 1 toughness, so Midnight Guard would kill it and survive (2 damage vs 3 toughness), preventing 4 damage while keeping Midnight Guard alive. Blocking Visionary results in both creatures dying. Additionally, multiple blockers could have been assigned to minimize total damage taken.",
      "action_taken": "Midnight Guard blocked Lightning Visionary (3/2), resulting in a mutual kill and taking 5 damage from unblocked attackers.",
      "better_line": "Block Giant Ladybug (4/1) with Midnight Guard (2/3) — Midnight Guard survives and Ladybug dies. Then optionally block Lightning Visionary with Kami of Ancient Law. Use Divine Verdict only if needed. This prevents more damage and preserves Midnight Guard.",
      "type": "blunder",
