      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 253,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 149,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Declined to sacrifice Kami of Ancient Law to destroy Crawling Sensation, which will generate incremental value (1/1 insect tokens and graveyard filling) every turn going forward. The sacrifice costs no mana and removes an ongoing threat.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, keeping Kami of Ancient Law as a 2/2 body on the battlefield.",
      "better_line": "Activate Kami of Ancient Law to destroy Crawling Sensation before it starts generating tokens on the opponent's next upkeep. The 2/2 body is less valuable than preventing an engine that creates tokens and fills the graveyard each turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 256,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 151,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined Crawling Sensation's upkeep mill trigger, which is essentially free value. Milling two cards could hit a land to create a 1/1 Insect token, and could put creatures in the graveyard to make the Moldgraf Millipede in hand larger. With 27 cards in library, decking is not a concern. There is virtually no downside to milling here.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to mill two cards from Crawling Sensation's upkeep trigger.",
      "better_line": "Accept the mill trigger (choose yes/True) to get a chance at a free 1/1 Insect token and potentially grow the future Moldgraf Millipede.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 264,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 157,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to discard Thriving Bluff to Nantuko Cultivator's ETB trigger. Discarding it would have given a +1/+1 counter on Cultivator (making it 3/3), drawn a card, AND triggered Crawling Sensation to create a 1/1 Insect token (land going to graveyard). That's significant value for one tapped land.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to discard zero lands to Nantuko Cultivator's ETB ability.",
      "better_line": "Discard Thriving Bluff to Nantuko Cultivator, getting a +1/+1 counter, drawing a card, and creating a 1/1 Insect token via Crawling Sensation. The card draw could find another land, and the board presence is more immediately valuable than a guaranteed tapped land drop.",
      "type": "blunder",
