      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 301,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 180,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "QwCdr Proud blocked only the Turntimber Basilisk (2/1 deathtouch) with the valuable Nantuko Cultivator 3/3, leaving the Canopy Baloth 6/5 unblocked to deal 6 damage (going from 10 to 4 life). The Insect Token 1/1 was available to chump-block the Basilisk (dying to deathtouch either way), and the Nantuko Cultivator could have blocked the Canopy Baloth (which has no trample), preventing all 6 damage. Both creatures would die either way, but the correct blocks would have taken 0 damage instead of 6.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked Turntimber Basilisk with Nantuko Cultivator, leaving Canopy Baloth 6/5 unblocked (taking 6 damage)",
      "better_line": "Block Turntimber Basilisk with Insect Token (expendable, dies to deathtouch anyway) and block Canopy Baloth with Nantuko Cultivator (no trample, so all damage prevented). Both blockers die but 0 damage taken instead of 6.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 305,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 182,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Llama4 Rules cast Divine Verdict during their own combat phase. The opponent has no untapped creatures to block, so there are no blocking creatures to target. The only legal targets are Llama4's own attacking creatures (Turntimber Basilisk and Canopy Baloth). Destroying their own attacker wastes a removal spell and throws away 8 damage that would have brought the opponent from 10 to 2 life — essentially a lethal attack wasted.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Divine Verdict during own combat, targeting one of their own attacking creatures.",
      "better_line": "Pass priority and let combat damage resolve. Turntimber Basilisk (2) + Canopy Baloth (6) = 8 damage would bring the opponent to 2 life, setting up lethal next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 306,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 183,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Llama4 Rules timed out with Valorous Stance in hand and 6 untapped lands while Divine Verdict was on the stack targeting one of their attackers. Valorous Stance could grant indestructible to save the targeted creature (likely Canopy Baloth, a 6/5), completely blanking the opponent's removal spell. Instead, they lost a creature for free.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out (no response) while Divine Verdict was on the stack, allowing a creature to be destroyed.",
      "better_line": "Cast Valorous Stance choosing 'Target creature gains indestructible until end of turn' on whichever creature Divine Verdict targets (preferably Canopy Baloth as the larger threat), saving the creature and wasting the opponent's 4 mana removal spell.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 307,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 184,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Chose to sacrifice Canopy Baloth (6/5 this turn, 4/3 base) to Divine Verdict instead of Turntimber Basilisk (2/1 deathtouch). This means only 2 damage gets through instead of 6, leaving opponent at 8 instead of 4. In a tight race at 9 vs 10 life, that 4-point swing is enormous. Additionally, Canopy Baloth is the larger body going forward (4/3 vs 2/1) and the player already has Arrest and Valorous Stance in hand for removal, reducing the need for deathtouch.",
      "action_taken": "Chose Canopy Baloth to be destroyed by Divine Verdict, saving Turntimber Basilisk",
      "better_line": "Choose Turntimber Basilisk to be destroyed, letting Canopy Baloth deal 6 damage (opponent to 4) and keeping the bigger 4/3 body for future turns",
      "type": "blunder",
