    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Player timed out and made no blocks against 7 damage worth of attackers while at 9 life. With Kami of Ancient Law (2/2) and Oashra Cultivator (0/3) available to block, they could have blocked Nantuko Cultivator with Oashra (preventing 3 damage, trading Oashra) and Lightning Visionary with Kami (preventing 2 damage, Kami survives as 2/2 vs 2/1), taking only 2 damage instead of 7. Going to 2 life instead of 7 life is devastating with Sethron, Hurloon General about to attack next turn.",
      "action_taken": "No response (timeout) - no blocks declared, taking 7 damage to go to 2 life.",
      "better_line": "Block Lightning Visionary (2/1) with Kami of Ancient Law (2/2) and block Nantuko Cultivator (3/3) with Oashra Cultivator (0/3). This prevents 5 damage, only taking 2 (from Ironshell Beetle and Insect Token), staying at 7 life. Kami survives the block.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 344,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 200,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Used Arrest (3 mana, partial answer) on Sethron instead of Valorous Stance (2 mana, complete removal). Arrest doesn't stop Sethron's triggered ability from creating 2/3 Minotaur tokens when other Minotaurs enter, while Valorous Stance destroys Sethron outright for less mana. At 2 life, the extra mana efficiency and complete removal matter significantly.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Arrest on Sethron for 3 mana, leaving it on the battlefield with its triggered token-creation ability still active.",
      "better_line": "Cast Valorous Stance targeting Sethron (toughness 4) for 2 mana to destroy it completely, then use remaining 3 mana to cast Arrest on another threat like Nantuko Cultivator (3/3) or hold mana open for Gideon's Lawkeeper activation next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 355,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 204,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "At 2 life facing Sethron's menace activation next turn, individual blockers have limited value since menace requires pairs. Kami of Ancient Law as a 2/2 blocker doesn't meaningfully help against menace threats. Meanwhile, the opponent has no untapped blockers, so Kami would deal 2 free damage (opponent to 4 instead of 6), which increases pressure and makes future burn/attacks more likely to close the game.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only Turntimber Basilisk for 2 damage, keeping Kami of Ancient Law back",
      "better_line": "Attack with both Turntimber Basilisk and Kami of Ancient Law for 4 total damage (opponent to 4 life), since single blockers are poor against menace and the 2 extra damage is essentially free",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 365,
      "player": "Llama4 Rules",
      "decision_index": 207,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Blocked Turntimber Basilisk (2/1 deathtouch) with Sethron, Hurloon General (4/4), losing their best creature. The opponent is at 2 life, and Sethron was key to attacking for lethal next turn. The Minotaur Token (2/3) was available as a much cheaper blocker, or they could simply take 2 damage (going to 6 life) and attack for lethal next turn with Sethron + other creatures.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked Turntimber Basilisk with Sethron, Hurloon General, losing the 4/4 legendary to deathtouch.",
      "better_line": "Either don't block (take 2 damage, go to 6 life, attack for lethal next turn with Sethron giving menace to minotaurs) or block with Minotaur Token (2/3) to preserve Sethron. With the opponent at 2 life, Sethron is the most important piece for closing the game.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 368,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 208,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Borderland Minotaur before playing Forest from hand. With Forest played first (7 untapped lands), after casting Minotaur (4 mana), 3 mana would remain - exactly enough to activate Sethron's {2}{R} ability to give all Minotaurs +1/+0, menace, and haste. Without playing Forest first, only 2 mana remains after casting, which is insufficient for Sethron's ability. The opponent is at 2 HP with only 2 potential blockers, so menace + haste on all Minotaurs would guarantee lethal.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Borderland Minotaur with 6 untapped lands, leaving only 2 mana available after casting.",
      "better_line": "Play Forest first, then cast Borderland Minotaur, leaving 3 mana available to activate Sethron's ability for menace and haste on all Minotaurs, guaranteeing lethal attack.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 380,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 217,
    }
  ],
